WEBVTT

00:01.920 --> 00:03.250
Amit!

00:04.780 --> 00:07.540
Lady Sariphi, Sir Lanteveldt.

00:08.960 --> 00:09.990
What's wrong?

00:10.400 --> 00:13.290
You haven't seemed yourself lately.

00:13.860 --> 00:16.680
Is it something to do with Captain Jormungand?

00:17.720 --> 00:23.090
I heard that the Royal Guard should 
already have returned by now.

00:23.460 --> 00:26.420
I'm beside myself with worry.

00:27.410 --> 00:30.570
The Guard's on campaign in Aiphos, right?

00:30.570 --> 00:33.630
The interspecies wars there 
have been going on forever.

00:34.010 --> 00:36.950
They should just let the locals go at it.

00:37.900 --> 00:39.630
Don't worry, Amit.

00:40.290 --> 00:43.850
Jormungand has your amulet to keep him safe.

00:44.460 --> 00:45.840
Lady Sariphi...

00:46.250 --> 00:48.180
I swear to return unscathed,

00:48.730 --> 00:51.880
so that I may repay you for 
your thousand prayers.

00:52.600 --> 00:55.430
So I'm sure he'll be fine. Okay?

00:58.610 --> 01:02.110
After me! First Platoon, defend the civilians!

01:02.400 --> 01:05.220
The rest of you, secure the objective at once!

01:07.110 --> 01:12.030
This was once Rattian land 
before you stole it from us!

01:12.030 --> 01:14.330
Justice is on our side!

01:16.980 --> 01:21.870
No cause justifies turning a blade 
against unarmed people!

01:22.270 --> 01:23.860
You face <i>me</i> now!

02:55.020 --> 03:00.030
Chance Meeting of a Boy and a Child

03:00.330 --> 03:04.500
The Royal Guard has returned 
from Aiphos! Open the gates!

03:11.110 --> 03:12.820
<i>Captain Jormungand...</i>

03:14.100 --> 03:18.180
I, Captain Jormungand of the 
Royal Guard of Ozmargo,

03:18.180 --> 03:21.420
have returned with 80 soldiers, sire.

03:21.660 --> 03:24.420
You have served me well. 
I will hear your report later.

03:24.890 --> 03:27.650
Today, you and your men may take your ease.

03:27.650 --> 03:32.000
<i>Thank goodness. They all 
made it home safe and sound.</i>

03:37.400 --> 03:41.200
This mission seems to have 
taken you longer than usual, Jor.

03:41.470 --> 03:45.260
I believe I asked you not to absent 
yourself overlong on campaign.

03:45.260 --> 03:49.120
And <i>I</i> asked <i>you</i> not to gripe 
as soon as I get back, Abi.

03:50.450 --> 03:51.950
Why, Princess Amit.

03:51.950 --> 03:53.410
U-Um...

03:53.410 --> 03:54.570
What perfect timing.

03:54.910 --> 03:55.540
What?

03:55.540 --> 04:00.310
I have something to tell you. 
Alone, if possible.

04:00.730 --> 04:03.010
May I have a moment of your time?

04:03.010 --> 04:05.710
Wh-What?!

04:25.590 --> 04:30.730
<i>Wh-What could Captain Jormungand 
have to say to me?</i>

04:30.730 --> 04:33.990
<i>O-Oh, dear. I mustn't get carried away.</i>

04:33.990 --> 04:37.470
<i>And yet I have so much to say to him, as well!</i>

04:37.470 --> 04:38.370
Princess Amit.

04:39.990 --> 04:40.620
For you.

04:43.110 --> 04:47.590
That is... the amulet I gave you.

04:47.590 --> 04:51.890
Yes. I wish to return it.

04:51.890 --> 04:52.800
What?

04:53.130 --> 04:57.080
D-Did you find it, um, a hindrance?

04:57.080 --> 04:58.790
Perish the thought.

04:58.790 --> 05:02.820
Though our mission was perilous, 
we all returned safely.

05:03.490 --> 05:05.320
I have no doubt your amulet protected us.

05:05.320 --> 05:09.560
Th-Then, well, if you don't mind,

05:10.110 --> 05:12.270
I'd rather you kept it with you.

05:12.940 --> 05:15.910
No, I am unworthy of it.

05:16.260 --> 05:17.580
Please,

05:17.580 --> 05:21.790
bestow this on someone for 
whom you care more deeply.

05:22.150 --> 05:23.030
Good day.

05:34.030 --> 05:36.760
What? Jormungand said that?

05:36.760 --> 05:39.820
Yes. He just returned my amulet.

05:39.820 --> 05:41.570
Oh, no. But why?

05:41.570 --> 05:44.660
'Cause he doesn't need it anymore. Why else?

05:44.660 --> 05:47.180
Lante! Mind your manners.

05:47.700 --> 05:50.280
Sir Lanteveldt is right.

05:51.010 --> 05:52.490
This must be

05:52.490 --> 05:55.090
Captain Jormungand's reply to me.

05:58.790 --> 05:59.580
Talk about gloomy.

05:59.920 --> 06:02.920
Anyway, I can't believe you 
two are so buddy-buddy.

06:03.290 --> 06:05.720
Of course we are. We're friends.

06:05.720 --> 06:07.160
Lady Sariphi...

06:07.500 --> 06:09.250
I just can't accept this!

06:10.180 --> 06:11.480
Lady Sariphi?!

06:15.650 --> 06:18.860
Princess Amit's amulet?

06:18.860 --> 06:21.590
If you don't need it anymore, 
I can't help that.

06:21.590 --> 06:24.350
But if you have another reason, 
please tell me what it is.

06:24.730 --> 06:27.560
Amit put her heart into making that amulet.

06:28.160 --> 06:29.090
So...

06:30.600 --> 06:34.510
I must beg your pardon, 
but I cannot answer that.

06:34.510 --> 06:36.440
It is a personal matter.

06:36.440 --> 06:40.670
Hold it! Don't be so stingy, 
Mr. Royal Guard.

06:41.090 --> 06:41.920
And you are?

06:42.170 --> 06:45.500
Lanteveldt, captain of the 
acting queen's personal guard.

06:45.500 --> 06:46.880
And don't you forget it.

06:47.080 --> 06:48.810
You lead the Queen's Guard?

06:48.810 --> 06:52.210
I see. So you're the one Abi—
the chancellor mentioned.

06:52.210 --> 06:54.260
<i>That insolent whelp is...</i>

06:54.730 --> 06:57.850
I can more or less guess what he said.

06:58.270 --> 07:01.440
But anyway, how about you and I...

07:01.640 --> 07:05.310
A d-duel?! Between Captain 
Jormungand and Sir Lanteveldt?!

07:05.620 --> 07:07.910
What could possess them to do such a thing?!

07:07.910 --> 07:12.650
We're not really sure. 
Lante challenged him out of the blue.

07:12.650 --> 07:13.290
Blue.

07:13.290 --> 07:16.230
Th-Then... where are they now?!

07:19.200 --> 07:24.560
Lanteveldt, was it? 
Why do you wish to battle me?

07:24.560 --> 07:27.150
My sword serves the king's will.

07:27.660 --> 07:31.680
Should you not wield your strength 
for your liege's sake, as well?

07:31.680 --> 07:35.350
My "liege" is looking down 
in the dumps because of you.

07:35.350 --> 07:37.900
So we're gonna fight, and if I win,

07:37.900 --> 07:40.370
I'm gonna make you answer 
Sariphi's question.

07:41.080 --> 07:44.410
This is my idea of loyalty. 
You got a problem with that?

07:44.410 --> 07:46.930
Give him his duel, Jormungand.

07:46.930 --> 07:47.720
Sire!

07:47.720 --> 07:49.230
I permit it.

07:49.650 --> 07:50.650
But...

07:50.910 --> 07:55.470
I've yet to see the captain 
of the Queen's Guard fight.

07:55.470 --> 07:59.860
If he can hold his own against you, 
then he should do the same in battle.

07:59.860 --> 08:01.870
Now Your Majesty's speaking my language.

08:01.870 --> 08:04.460
How dare you address His Majesty 
so flippantly after—

08:03.880 --> 08:05.210
Very well.

08:05.990 --> 08:11.210
If it is my king's command, then I, 
Jormungand, humbly accept this challenge

08:11.560 --> 08:13.420
from Captain Lanteveldt 
of the Queen's Guard.

08:15.970 --> 08:18.000
Oh, no! They've already started!

08:22.910 --> 08:24.050
Sire,

08:24.050 --> 08:26.530
why did you allow this duel?

08:26.830 --> 08:29.010
I wish you'd stopped them.

08:29.010 --> 08:31.730
I wanted to make sure of something.

08:35.860 --> 08:40.370
Don't get careless. Not everyone 
you fight will stand on ceremony.

08:40.620 --> 08:43.620
Yes, I could say the same to you.

08:44.010 --> 08:44.780
Huh?

08:47.350 --> 08:49.000
Stop! We have a winner!

08:51.320 --> 08:52.660
Wait, that counted?!

08:52.660 --> 08:53.960
No fair! That's cheating!

08:54.300 --> 08:55.580
I see.

08:56.620 --> 08:58.380
Did you figure something out?

08:58.730 --> 09:01.610
Yes. I suspect that he is...

09:01.610 --> 09:04.190
One more time! I want a rematch!

09:07.490 --> 09:08.990
Captain Jormungand.

09:12.800 --> 09:13.910
Your Highness?

09:14.260 --> 09:15.860
How may I help you?

09:20.580 --> 09:22.730
P-Pardon me.

09:24.640 --> 09:26.220
I knew it! You <i>are</i> wounded!

09:27.490 --> 09:28.410
Um...

09:28.780 --> 09:34.760
Take this Murgan salve. It's well-suited 
for Reptilian constitutions.

09:34.760 --> 09:39.150
How did you know? I tried to 
hide it even from my own men.

09:39.480 --> 09:42.350
Lady Sariphi told me.

09:42.720 --> 09:47.220
His Majesty said that Jormungand's 
swordplay seemed off to him.

09:47.220 --> 09:50.850
He wondered if the captain might be hurt.

09:51.550 --> 09:53.200
The king said that?

09:53.470 --> 09:57.670
You received that wound 
on the campaign, didn't you?

09:57.670 --> 09:59.410
That's why you returned the...

10:01.690 --> 10:02.990
Forgive me.

10:02.990 --> 10:07.060
I'm so sorry that my amulet failed you.

10:07.060 --> 10:08.720
You're wrong.

10:09.060 --> 10:15.790
I returned your amulet because 
I wished to spare you this distress.

10:16.320 --> 10:17.050
What?

10:17.050 --> 10:24.300
I blundered in the course of my duty 
and failed to repay your kindness.

10:25.040 --> 10:30.930
As long as I held your amulet, any harm 
I suffered would wound your heart.

10:30.930 --> 10:36.190
And so I returned it to you, 
despite the discourtesy.

10:37.240 --> 10:43.530
So, Amit, this is just my guess, 
but I think Jormungand must have...

10:45.790 --> 10:48.740
Captain Jormungand, I...

10:49.290 --> 10:52.640
I have no exceptional talent or strength.

10:52.640 --> 10:58.230
So I gave you that amulet 
because it was the most I could do.

10:58.630 --> 11:01.340
You risk your life in battle.

11:01.830 --> 11:05.950
So from now on, I will risk mine, as well.

11:06.570 --> 11:10.720
I'll become so strong that 
nothing can shake me.

11:10.720 --> 11:13.180
So... So...

11:13.640 --> 11:17.910
Please take this with you once more!

11:28.450 --> 11:30.340
Ugh! This sucks!

11:30.340 --> 11:32.010
I can't stand it!

11:31.170 --> 11:33.220
You put up a good fight.

11:33.220 --> 11:37.410
Yes, His Majesty said that you'd 
make a good guard captain.

11:37.670 --> 11:41.620
Saying I held my own against an 
injured guy isn't a compliment.

11:41.850 --> 11:46.260
Um, Lady Sariphi, how could you tell?

11:46.260 --> 11:47.030
Huh?

11:47.470 --> 11:53.100
That Captain Jormungand returned 
the amulet for my sake, I mean.

11:53.100 --> 11:56.600
Just a hunch. I couldn't be sure.

11:56.600 --> 11:59.820
But if His Majesty had done it, 
I'm sure that would be why.

12:00.390 --> 12:03.030
My goodness, Lady Sariphi!

12:03.030 --> 12:05.980
Ridiculous. You just wanna 
brag about your love life?

12:06.330 --> 12:09.670
Still, you've got a real jumble 
of people around you.

12:10.330 --> 12:13.150
You've got me, a Hyenian, 
leading your guard.

12:13.540 --> 12:18.330
Your friend's a Reptilian princess, 
your servants are Cyclopians,

12:18.330 --> 12:20.890
and your holy beast is this thing.

12:20.890 --> 12:23.390
Who're you calling "this thing," nincompoop?!

12:23.850 --> 12:27.950
And to top it off, the king of 
beasts is marrying a human.

12:27.950 --> 12:32.840
You're right, but I hope that 
all this will be normal someday.

12:33.250 --> 12:36.740
That all of us, no matter the species, 
accept that we're different,

12:36.740 --> 12:38.610
but also the same deep down.

12:39.260 --> 12:41.030
That's what I hope for.

12:41.730 --> 12:44.150
Now <i>that's</i> a pie in the sky.

12:44.490 --> 12:45.800
That's true.

12:46.450 --> 12:52.810
<i>Yes, the hatred between beasts and humans 
is more than simple preference.</i>

12:53.610 --> 13:00.440
<i>Even now, I know people out there are 
suffering from wounds that I can't heal.</i>

13:00.790 --> 13:03.760
Are you really leaving?

13:03.760 --> 13:09.860
Yeah. I hear beasts are snatching kids 
farther east along the border.

13:10.360 --> 13:13.550
As a professional beast hunter, 
I can't ignore that.

13:13.890 --> 13:16.260
I see. Take care, then.

13:16.260 --> 13:18.430
Don't do anything too rash.

13:18.800 --> 13:20.500
Thanks for everything, Gramps.

13:21.070 --> 13:22.070
See you!

13:33.300 --> 13:34.450
Ilya!

13:34.970 --> 13:36.530
I'll see you again, won't I?

13:42.760 --> 13:43.700
<i>Beasts!</i>

13:43.960 --> 13:46.640
Whoever you are, get out of our way!

13:51.330 --> 13:52.570
You won't get away!

13:57.940 --> 14:00.060
Hey, kid. Are you hurt?

14:00.410 --> 14:03.440
N-No, I'm fine.

14:03.760 --> 14:05.780
I've got a hard head!

14:07.620 --> 14:09.650
Huh? A human?

14:11.510 --> 14:16.390
Th-Thanks, mister. You saved me!

14:16.390 --> 14:19.900
I'm Maalo. What's your name?

14:21.120 --> 14:21.810
Hey.

14:21.810 --> 14:22.500
Stay back!

14:27.180 --> 14:29.940
Killing a kid like you is a waste of time.

14:29.940 --> 14:31.810
I'll let you go, so disappear.

14:31.810 --> 14:33.720
I don't know how to.

14:33.720 --> 14:36.630
It means go home! To your own country!

14:36.630 --> 14:37.960
I don't know how.

14:37.960 --> 14:38.440
What?!

14:38.670 --> 14:42.390
I got kidnapped, so I don't 
know the way home.

14:45.690 --> 14:47.330
Hey, mister!

14:47.330 --> 14:50.650
Are you really going to take me home?!

14:51.060 --> 14:54.200
I just told you to follow me 
since I'm headed for the border.

14:54.600 --> 14:56.840
And don't walk so close.

14:56.840 --> 14:58.850
Okay! I can get home, then.

14:58.850 --> 15:00.210
Thanks, mister.

15:00.210 --> 15:02.180
Stop calling me that.

15:02.570 --> 15:07.500
You're a weird kid. What kind 
of beast thanks a human?

15:07.500 --> 15:09.130
Huh? Why wouldn't I?

15:09.130 --> 15:14.460
My mom always tells me to say thank you 
when someone does something nice for me.

15:14.800 --> 15:17.180
Do humans not say thank you?

15:18.640 --> 15:20.890
Hey! Wait for me!

15:20.890 --> 15:25.320
<i>What's wrong with this beast? 
He talks like a human.</i>

15:27.810 --> 15:28.900
Hey, kid.

15:31.420 --> 15:32.500
He's gone?!

15:32.930 --> 15:34.700
I barely took my eyes off him.

15:34.700 --> 15:36.810
Don't tell me he got kidnapped aga—

15:39.620 --> 15:41.500
Ow!

15:41.500 --> 15:43.550
Don't wander off, you little brat!

15:43.550 --> 15:45.120
I told you to follow me!

15:45.400 --> 15:46.580
Mister!

15:46.580 --> 15:47.630
Stop that!

15:47.630 --> 15:50.290
Not listening is probably 
what got you kidnapped!

15:50.290 --> 15:52.360
I'm sorry. It's just...

15:52.680 --> 15:56.940
I've never seen such pretty 
flowers and weird bugs before.

15:56.940 --> 16:00.050
Do humans always live in places like this?

16:00.050 --> 16:02.010
That must be nice.

16:02.960 --> 16:06.180
Hey, why did those guys bring you here?

16:06.790 --> 16:08.870
Why would beasts kidnap a beast?

16:08.870 --> 16:09.810
Huh?

16:10.200 --> 16:14.910
Well, uh, lots of kids are 
getting taken lately.

16:14.910 --> 16:17.080
First they get sold to humans,

16:17.080 --> 16:20.570
then they get "stuffed" 
or put in "freak shows."

16:20.870 --> 16:26.790
<i>So the beast kidnappers I 
heard about work for humans?</i>

16:24.490 --> 16:27.390
I wonder if "freak shows" are fun...

16:27.390 --> 16:29.710
<i>Humans treating beasts like playthings?</i>

16:30.640 --> 16:31.750
<i>It's almost like</i>

16:32.750 --> 16:34.140
<i>what happened back then.</i>

16:35.750 --> 16:36.980
Mister?

16:37.270 --> 16:38.880
Are you hurt?

16:38.880 --> 16:39.680
Don't touch me!

16:47.460 --> 16:48.730
What are you doing?

16:48.990 --> 16:51.910
Y-You said not to touch.

16:52.950 --> 16:57.880
My mom always rubs me 
when I've got a boo-boo.

16:57.880 --> 17:00.400
So I'm rubbing you without touching.

17:00.400 --> 17:02.410
Boo-boo, get better!

17:02.410 --> 17:03.380
Get better!

17:03.380 --> 17:04.250
Get—

17:05.220 --> 17:07.150
There! There it is!

17:07.150 --> 17:10.890
I've had it with these beasts 
and their sloppy work.

17:10.890 --> 17:12.910
They took the money and ran.

17:13.390 --> 17:14.470
<i>Humans.</i>

17:14.970 --> 17:16.060
Who are you?

17:16.060 --> 17:20.800
We serve a certain noble personage. 
That's all I can tell you.

17:20.800 --> 17:23.780
That beast is our prey.

17:24.170 --> 17:26.310
<i>...they get sold to humans...</i>

17:26.310 --> 17:27.230
<i>These must be...</i>

17:27.230 --> 17:30.230
Now, hand it over.

17:32.320 --> 17:35.450
Hm? That tattoo on your left cheek...

17:35.820 --> 17:39.140
You must be that wanderer 
who hunts beasts in these parts.

17:39.140 --> 17:41.780
Are you after this one, too?

17:42.550 --> 17:43.540
I'm...

17:46.520 --> 17:47.700
not involved.

17:48.270 --> 17:50.660
I don't care what happens to him.

17:50.660 --> 17:52.280
Glad to hear it.

17:52.280 --> 17:52.880
Huh?

17:53.180 --> 17:55.170
Where are we going?

17:55.170 --> 17:58.210
To a master who'll take 
real good care of you.

17:58.440 --> 17:59.410
What?

17:59.410 --> 18:02.800
No! I wanna go home!

18:02.800 --> 18:05.510
Stop! Let go of me!

18:05.510 --> 18:07.470
I wanna go home!

18:06.120 --> 18:07.470
Settle down!

18:07.880 --> 18:11.680
Stop it! Mom!

18:12.360 --> 18:18.660
<i>Why should I care if he lives, dies, 
gets stuffed, or ends up in a freak show?</i>

18:19.030 --> 18:21.320
<i>As long as he's out of my hair, then...</i>

18:21.320 --> 18:22.780
No! Stop!

18:22.780 --> 18:24.550
Shut your mouth and stop whining!

18:22.780 --> 18:24.550
I don't wanna go!

18:25.090 --> 18:29.560
Help, mister!

18:34.000 --> 18:35.850
Wh-What's the big idea?!

18:35.850 --> 18:39.020
Couldn't resist the money 
this thing'll fetch?!

18:39.960 --> 18:41.540
Don't think I'm like you.

18:42.150 --> 18:44.770
I hate beasts' guts.

18:45.090 --> 18:48.010
But bastards like you,

18:48.360 --> 18:53.180
who toy with people's lives, 
piss me off even more.

18:53.440 --> 18:54.560
What?!

18:54.560 --> 18:58.080
If you get in our way, 
we'll make you regret it!

19:03.040 --> 19:03.960
Don't just stand there!

19:04.230 --> 19:05.410
Run for it!

19:07.870 --> 19:08.830
Idiot!

19:10.070 --> 19:13.010
Don't pick on him!

19:13.360 --> 19:14.000
Are you...

19:14.000 --> 19:15.460
Hey, be careful.

19:15.460 --> 19:17.100
It's worth nothing if we kill it.

19:17.100 --> 19:17.880
I know.

19:29.890 --> 19:31.770
I'll only say this once.

19:31.770 --> 19:34.820
If you value your lives 
more than pocket change,

19:34.820 --> 19:36.530
then get lost right now.

19:37.040 --> 19:39.200
O-Okay, you win!

19:39.200 --> 19:40.770
You can have that thing!

19:48.570 --> 19:50.500
You should've minded your own business.

19:50.890 --> 19:54.010
I can't live with being in debt to a beast.

19:54.010 --> 19:56.180
But we're even now, got it?

19:56.180 --> 19:58.470
I didn't lend you anything.

19:58.470 --> 19:59.210
Listen, you...

20:01.280 --> 20:05.590
<i>It may be small now, but it'll 
kill humans when it's grown.</i>

20:05.590 --> 20:07.580
<i>That's just how they are.</i>

20:08.250 --> 20:11.370
<i>But not all beasts want that.</i>

20:13.240 --> 20:17.330
There are all kinds of beasts. 
Some are nice, and some are scared.

20:17.960 --> 20:19.740
<i>Just like humans.</i>

20:23.310 --> 20:26.470
<i>I say it when someone does 
something nice for me.</i>

20:26.470 --> 20:28.350
<i>Do humans not?</i>

20:29.860 --> 20:32.510
What I mean to say is... thanks.

20:34.990 --> 20:37.930
That's the way. You're welcome!

20:41.440 --> 20:46.010
<i>I won't change. My hatred 
of beasts will last forever.</i>

20:46.770 --> 20:47.840
<i>But, Sariphi...</i>

20:48.740 --> 20:56.970
<i>Maybe you had a point, at least 
about the beasts you got to know.</i>

20:57.860 --> 20:59.660
<i>Beasts like this little guy.</i>

21:02.800 --> 21:05.690
Go on. Cross that mountain, 
and you're in beast country.

21:05.690 --> 21:08.060
The sky's normal again!

21:08.060 --> 21:11.710
I can't go any farther, 
so figure out the rest yourself.

21:11.710 --> 21:13.200
I will! Thank you.

21:13.530 --> 21:16.960
Come play with me in 
Ozmargo sometime, mister!

21:16.960 --> 21:18.530
If I feel like it.

21:19.350 --> 21:21.000
You've got to!

21:21.000 --> 21:23.970
See you, mister! Bye-bye!

21:24.280 --> 21:27.450
I said, bye-bye!

21:40.780 --> 21:43.590
Bye-bye!

22:50.090 --> 22:53.710
We didn't count on the 
Royal Guard getting involved.

22:53.710 --> 22:55.540
But next time...

22:55.540 --> 23:00.220
You know, I hear the Blood Pact Corps in 
Maasya has announced that it's disbanding.

23:00.530 --> 23:04.520
They were the biggest 
anti-monarchist group around there.

23:04.520 --> 23:06.510
Hah! Cowards!

23:06.510 --> 23:11.120
I always knew that it would fall to us, 
the Black Stars, to topple the king!

23:11.510 --> 23:14.380
You don't change much, either.

23:14.380 --> 23:15.950
Wh-Who goes there?!

23:15.950 --> 23:18.430
Did the king send you?!

23:18.430 --> 23:21.300
That's right. From now on,

23:21.770 --> 23:24.620
you're soldiers in His Majesty's service.

23:26.630 --> 23:29.520
The anti-monarchists have 
all gone quiet at once?

23:29.520 --> 23:31.960
As if at a signal.

23:31.960 --> 23:35.310
That seems like a blessing, but I wonder.

23:35.630 --> 23:38.900
Indeed. Something stinks.

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
Invasion and the Wolf Without a Kingdom
